# CLAUDE.md

This file provides guidance to Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with code in this repository.

## Operating rules — load before writing code

Two operating specs govern all code in this repo. Read them before generating code and apply them **as you write** — they are the rules the `code-review:code-review` skill blocks on:

- **`docs/CODING_PRACTICES.md`** (cited as **CP §n**) — TypeScript boundary safety, NestJS, Next.js App Router + React 19, OWASP-aligned security, cross-cutting logic-bug patterns. Apply **CP §7** to the changed scope, run the required checks and report the evidence; add another review only for a named unresolved risk.
- **`docs/NEW_PROJECT_BEST_PRACTICES.md`** (cited as **BP §n**) — stack defaults and day-one decisions. When a task is underspecified, take the BP default instead of inventing one; when you deliberately diverge, say so and why.

**Behaviour under ambiguity** (bias toward caution over speed; for trivial tasks, use judgment):

- **Resolve ambiguity at the right level.** Read the source and existing decisions, make routine reversible calls, and state material assumptions. Ask only when different readings lead to materially different work the user must choose; do not ask again for existing authorization.
- **Simplicity first.** Minimum change that solves the problem. No speculative features or abstractions.
- **Surgical changes.** Don't "improve" adjacent code; match existing style; mention unrelated problems instead of fixing them. Every changed line traces to the request.
- **Finish against concrete criteria.** Define the required artifact and acceptance checks, complete the requested scope, and stop when those criteria are met. Repeat checks when changes, failures or unresolved concerns require it.

